{
    "name": "[Baseline] - WIN - D - Network Authentication Hardening",
    "description": "Makes network authentication less susceptible to abuse: the system account uses the computer identity for NTLM, PKU2U with online identities is closed, LDAP traffic requests signing, the Kerberos client supports armoring and NetBIOS names are no longer resolved via broadcast. Baseline assignment: none by default — pilot group SEC-Baseline-Pilot first. Source: CIS v4 Windows 11 L1 (IntuneAdmin CISv4 profiles) and the Microsoft Security Baseline for Windows 11 — values verified against the settings catalog definitions; PKU2U deliberately deviates from the IntuneAdmin value.",
